From 35cb41c789b132657301004a03fbee06936f36dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qingh097 <qingh097@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:47:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Three-view policy support

The policy consumed a single ego camera while Image3F generated three synchronized views,
so two of the three were rendered and discarded. Views are now tiled vertically into one
image and the whole stack is fed to the ResNet:

    [ head_color ]  108x192
    [ hand_left  ]  108x192   ->  vision_obs (324, 192, 3)
    [ hand_right ]  108x192

Enabled per experiment with cameras.policy_views plus policy_view_count; both default to
the single ego view, so existing configs are unaffected.

- isaacsim.get_policy_view_stack(): tiles the conditioning cameras (already rendered for
  the renderer) downsampled to the policy resolution. No new cameras.
- legged_robot_base: prefers the stack, falls back to the ego camera.
- distill_trainer_videogen: tiles the generated views in the DAgger relabel and the
  per-view rgb_gen__<view> keys in the offline BC path, in policy_views order, so
  ray-traced and generated observations share one layout.
- camera_resolution now scales by len(policy_views) at all five derivations (two PPO
  bases, two distill trainers). It feeds the vision_obs storage shape and the obs_dim
  assertion, so scaling it centrally keeps every consumer consistent.
- history_handler: the RGB buffer built its shape from camera_resolutions, bypassing
  obs_dims; it now scales too.
- obs config: RGB dims multiply by  (default 1) instead of being
  overridden per experiment -- overriding obs_dims replaces the whole list and drops
  every other observation dimension.
- new configs wsdpt_image_dagger_3view and wsdpt_videogen_offline_bc_3view, each
  self-contained: Hydra resolves an included config's defaults relative to the including
  config's group, so these exp configs cannot be nested.

Single-view checkpoints cannot be warm-started into a 3-view policy. Offline BC also
needs the dataset re-rendered, since existing chunks carry only the primary rgb_gen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
